Table full name: bigquery-public-data.san_francisco_transit_muni.calendar
Column name: service_id Type: STRING Description: Unique identifier for a set of dates when service is available for one or more routes
Column name: service_desc Type: STRING Description: Text description of service category
Column name: sunday Type: BOOL Description: Indicates whether the service is valid for all Sundays operating on the agency is using normal schedules and fare categories
Column name: monday Type: BOOL Description: Indicates whether the service is valid for all Sundays operating on the agency is using normal schedules and fare categories
Column name: tuesday Type: BOOL Description: Indicates whether the service is valid for all Sundays operating on the agency is using normal schedules and fare categories
Column name: wednesday Type: BOOL Description: Indicates whether the service is valid for all Sundays operating on the agency is using normal schedules and fare categories
Column name: thursday Type: BOOL Description: Indicates whether the service is valid for all Sundays operating on the agency is using normal schedules and fare categories
Column name: friday Type: BOOL Description: Indicates whether the service is valid for all Sundays operating on the agency is using normal schedules and fare categories
Column name: saturday Type: BOOL Description: Indicates whether the service is valid for all Sundays operating on the agency is using normal schedules and fare categories
Column name: exceptions Type: DATE Description: Specifies a particular date when this service is not available. This is typically during holidays, special events, etc. If applicable, the operating service for the day is indicated in replacement_service. Format for the date is YYYY-MM-DD
Column name: exception_type Type: BOOL Description: Indicates whether service is available on the date specified in the exceptions field. The following are valid values for this field:  - TRUE: Service will be operating during the date listed in the column exceptions -  FALSE: Service will not be operating during the date listed in the column exceptions
